      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-3),\\,\\sqrt{2t},\\,{t}^{5}⟩$ at $t=2?$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=2$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2}-3),\\sqrt{2(2)},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1),\\sqrt{4},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,32⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=2$ is the vector $⟨0,2,32⟩.$",
