      "math_academy_id": "q-348674",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨{2}^{t-1},\\,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨{2}^{0},\\,\\frac{4}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
